# gRPC Studio UI Rules

These rules apply when creating or modifying **gRPC Studio** UI:
`src/features/grpc/`, `src/styles/grpc-studio.css`, and related selectors in `src/shared/selectors/grpc.ts`.

**Design tokens:** Follow [`.cursor/rules/ui-design-system.mdc`](ui-design-system.mdc) — use `var(--bg)`, `var(--surface)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--text)`, `var(--text-muted)`, `var(--primary)`. Never hardcode hex/rgba for theme surfaces.

**Phase 1 vs mockup gaps:** See [`docs/plan/future/grpc/grpc-studio-plan.md`](../../docs/plan/future/grpc/grpc-studio-plan.md) § Phase 1 vs mockup gap and **§ Phase 4J — Protocol UI/UX Parity** for TLS/Auth divergence remediation. See [`docs/guides/grpc-phase1-runbook.md`](../../docs/guides/grpc-phase1-runbook.md) § UI mockup parity.

**⚠️ Divergence rule (Phase 4J):** Do **not** add inline PEM editors or page-level TLS blocks. TLS must use **`GrpcTlsConfigModal`** via **`GrpcTlsPanel`** (tri-mode + secret masking — not shared `TlsConfigModal`). Connection bar must expose TLS + Auth badges per mockup `01`.

