## Phase 4 — `04-auth-tls.html`

Reference for connection bar completion and settings panels.

> **Shipped vs mockup:** Phase 4 logic + **4J-A/B/C/D UI** — connection bar badges, TLS modal, auth pills, full settings drawer nav (incl. Compression, Health, K8s stub, Transport). See [`grpc-studio-plan.md`](../../docs/plan/future/grpc/grpc-studio-plan.md) § Phase 4J.

| Mockup region | Expected behavior | 4J sub-phase |
|---|---|---|
| Connection bar | Status dot (connected/disconnected), TLS badge, Auth badge, Connect/Disconnect, Save Profile | **4J-A ✅** badges + target; **Phase 1 ✅** Connect/Cancel probe toggle |
| TLS entry | Bar **`tls-badge`** → modal — **not** inline page panel | **4J-B ✅** — `GrpcTlsConfigModal` + headless `GrpcTlsPanel` host |
| Auth entry | Bar Auth chip + settings nav; keep bottom Auth tab (dual entry) | **4J-A/C ✅** — pills + drawer Auth nav; badge focuses tab |
| Settings layout | Left nav (`settings-nav`) + scrollable main (`settings-main`) | **4J-C/D ✅** full nav |
| TLS / mTLS | Three-mode selector (disabled / TLS / mTLS), cert upload areas, mTLS indicator | **4J-B** in modal |
| Authentication | Type tabs: None, Bearer, Basic, API Key, OAuth2, GCE; per-type form panels | **4J-B** — pills + two-tone rows |
| Call settings | Deadline/timeout, keepalive, max message size | **4J-C/D ✅** deadline editable; keepalive/max size disabled rows |
| Compression | gzip/deflate/none selector | **4J-D ✅** |
| Health check | `grpc.health.v1` probe UI | **4J-D ✅** |
| K8s port-forward | Context/namespace/service selectors, auto-forward toggle | **4J-D ✅** stub (kubectl deferred) |
| Transport | Native vs gRPC-Web toggle (Phase 10 extends this panel) | **4J-D ✅** read-only Express active |

Follow **two-tone form row** pattern from `ui-design-system.mdc` for all settings cards.

**Anti-patterns (do not ship):**
- Always-visible PEM textareas on the main studio page (`GrpcStudioPage` inline TLS block)
- Auth type as native `<select>` when pills match GQL/mockup 04
- gRPC-only TLS CSS that duplicates `TlsConfigModal` / `ws-tls-*` rules

